From: superslor <289523157+superslor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:20:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] CUDA FA: skip KV blocks that a unified KV cache fully
 masks

With --kv-unified a sequence's cells are interleaved with the other sequences', so fully masked blocks
sit inside the KV range where the tail trim cannot reach them. A bitmap of live 256-cell blocks lets the
vec and tile kernels skip the dead ones; output is unchanged. Also bounds the mask scan to the real token
count (it read one row past the mask at 3 tokens with ncols1 4).

V100, Qwen3 hybrid Q6_K, -c 262144 -np 4: a 93-token request with a 67k conversation parked in another
slot 18.18 -> 25.05 t/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TS8XWm5bp2cWmYvbQ5tTBK
